{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--kamuy-means-god","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The noun kamuy means 'god' or 'spirit'.","ja":"名詞 kamuy は「神」または「精霊」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kamuy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0003-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0011-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--kar-gather-wild-plants","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--flora"],"statement":{"en":"The transitive verb kar is used with the meaning 'to gather or pick edible wild plants' in addition to 'to make'.","ja":"他動詞 kar は「作る」という意味のほかに、食用植物や山菜を「採る」という意味でも用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0112-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0125-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-word-arke-means-one-of-a-pair","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The word ʔarke means one of a pair of items.","ja":"ʔarke は「二つで一組をなすもののうちの片方」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ʔarke","arke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kirikae1997@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0011-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-more-general-word-for-to-work-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The more general word for 'to work' is 'nepki', whereas 'monrayke' is mainly used in oral literature and frequently functions nominally.","ja":"「働く」を意味するより一般的な語は nepki であり，monrayke は主に口承文芸で使われ，名詞的に用いられることが多い。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["nepki","monrayke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0213-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--t-ri-is-a-pole-used-to-navigate","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"túri is a pole used to navigate a boat, and boats are mainly operated with túri in places of normal depth, whereas assap 'oar' is used in deep places where the pole cannot reach the riverbed.","ja":"túri は舟を操るための「竿」のことであり、普通の深さの場所では主に túri で舟を操り、深くて竿が川底に届かないような場所では assap「かい」を使う。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["túri","assap"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0257-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-phrase-aynu-osarkes-is-used-as-an","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase aynu osarkes is used as an insult meaning 'poor fellow / pauper'.","ja":"aynu osarkes は「貧乏野郎」という悪口として用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["aynu osarkes"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0310-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-verb-nise-means-to-scoop-with-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The verb nise means 'to scoop (with a tool)'.","ja":"動詞 nise は「(道具で)すくう」という意味である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["nise"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0314-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--according-to-the-speaker-itakkasi-means-to-not","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"According to the speaker, itakkasi means 'to not listen to what someone says, to disobey'.","ja":"話者によれば、itakkasi は「言うことをきかない」ことである。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["itakkasi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0317-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-stem-ruy-alone-means-to-be-intense","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The stem ruy alone means 'to be intense, to become intense'.","ja":"ruy だけでも「激しい，激しくなる」という意味である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ruy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0319-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-verbs-pan-weak-in-taste-thin-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The verbs pan 'weak in taste / thin' and nupur 'strong in taste / thick' are also used in the sense of a god's spiritual power being weak or strong.","ja":"pan は「(味が) 薄い」、nupur は「(味が) 濃い」という意味の語であるが、神としての力が強い、弱い、という意味でも用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["referring to divine power"]},"forms":["pan","nupur"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0324-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-phrase-nupur-kur-literally-means-thick-person","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase nupur kur literally means 'thick person', but is used with the meaning of 'a person with spiritual power, a person with divinatory ability'.","ja":"nupur kur は文字通りには「濃い人」であるが、「霊力のある人、占いの能力のある人」という意味で用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["nupur kur"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0324-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--according-to-speakers-isoytak-means-to-narrate-what","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"According to speakers, isoytak means to narrate what one has heard or seen.","ja":"話者によれば isoytak は「聞いたり見たりしたことを語る」という意味である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["isoytak"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0330-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-verb-satsatu-means-to-dry-but-it","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The verb satsatu means 'to dry', but it is used for food items such as meat, fish, and wild plants, and is not used when referring to hanging up laundry.","ja":"satsatu は「干す」という意味だが、肉、魚、山菜などの食料について用い、洗濯物を干すと言う場合には使わない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["satsatu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0341-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-verb-satke-to-dry-can-be-used","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The verb satke 'to dry' can be used both when drying food and when hanging out laundry.","ja":"satke は食料を干す場合にも洗濯物を干す場合にもどちらにも使える。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["satke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0341-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--ramuriten-means-rejoice-be-glad","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"ramuriten means 'rejoice / be glad'.","ja":"ramuriten は「喜ぶ」という意味である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ramuriten"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0367-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--eyaykopuntek-and-ukoeyaykopuntek-also-means-rejoice-but-it","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"eyaykopuntek (and ukoeyaykopuntek) also means 'rejoice', but it has fewer examples than ramuriten and is often used for rejoicing over receiving things or the arrival of game.","ja":"eyaykopuntek（uko- が付いた ukoeyaykopuntek という形式もある）は「喜ぶ」という意味を表し、ramuriten に比べて例は少ないが、物をもらったり獲物がやって来たことを喜ぶ場合が多い。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["eyaykopuntek","ukoeyaykopuntek"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0367-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-verb-etunne-or-etune-means-to-hate","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis"],"statement":{"en":"The verb etunne (or etune) means 'to hate it', 'not want to', 'be annoying', or 'to dislike it'.","ja":"動詞 etunne（または etune）は「それを嫌う」「嫌がる」「うるさがる」などを意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["etunne","etune"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0039-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-noun-kema-leg-foot-is-primarily-used","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--body-parts"],"statement":{"en":"The noun kema 'leg, foot' is primarily used in reference to humans, whereas cikir is primarily used for non-humans such as crabs, spiders, horses, and utensils.","ja":"名詞 kema「足」は主に人間に関して言い、cikir はカニ、クモ、ウマ、器物など人間以外の足について主として用いる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kema","cikir"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0272-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-verb-nuwap-refers-to-groaning-in-childbirth","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--body-parts"],"statement":{"en":"The verb nuwap refers to groaning in childbirth or from abdominal pain.","ja":"お産や腹痛でうなることを nuwap と言う。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["nuwap"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0319-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-noun-phrase-kim-un-kamuy-literally-means","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"The noun phrase 'kim un kamuy' literally means 'god in the mountain', but usually refers to a bear.","ja":"kim un kamuy は文字通りには「山にいる神」という意味であるが，普通は動物のクマのことを指す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kim un kamuy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0035-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-word-kamuy-means-god-but-is-also","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"The word 'kamuy' means 'god', but is also frequently used alone to refer to a bear.","ja":"kamuy は「神」という意味だが，クマのことをただ kamuy と言うこともよくある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kamuy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0035-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-word-ocakaype-refers-according-to-the-consultant","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"The word ocakaype refers, according to the consultant, to a salmon with a thin tail.","ja":"話者によれば、ocakaype は「尻尾が細いサケ」を意味する。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ocakaype"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0309-03","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-word-kamuy-is-a-generic-term-for","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"The word kamuy is a generic term for animals and is also used to designate bears.","ja":"kamuy という単語は動物の総称であり、熊を指すためにも用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kamuy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0011-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--in-hokkaido-ainu-any-hairless-animal-specimen-was","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido Ainu, any hairless animal specimen was designated as tontone 'like a tonto'.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語では、毛のない動物標本はすべてtontone（tontoのようである）と呼ばれた。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["tontone"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shiraishitangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0046-09","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--saru-ainu-rik-means-whale-meat","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"Saru Ainu riká means 'whale meat'.","ja":"沙流アイヌ語のrikáは「鯨の肉」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["riká"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0036-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--in-kuril-ainu-materials-rika-is-recorded-with","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"In Kuril Ainu materials, rika is recorded with the meanings 'whale meat' and 'whale'.","ja":"千島アイヌ語の資料において、rikaは「鯨の肉」および「鯨」の意味で記録されている。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:kuril"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["rika"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0036-03","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--sakhalin-ainu-has-a-form-irika-tentatively-glossed","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"Sakhalin Ainu has a form 'irika tentatively glossed as 'dolphin'.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語には「イルカ」を意味する可能性がある形式'irikaが存在する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["'irika"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0036-04","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--in-hokkaido-and-sakhalin-ainu-rika-means-white","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido and Sakhalin Ainu, rika means 'white fat under the skin of a whale'.","ja":"北海道および樺太のアイヌ語において、rikaは「鯨の皮下の白身（脂肪）」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["rika"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0036-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--in-the-s-ya-dialect-of-hokkaido-ainu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--fauna"],"statement":{"en":"In the Sōya dialect of Hokkaido Ainu, rika means 'white fat under the skin of a whale'.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語宗谷方言において、rikaは「鯨の皮下の白身（脂肪）」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["Sōya dialect"]},"forms":["rika"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0036-06","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--ainu-strictly-differentiates-between-two-types-of-grass","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--flora"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu strictly differentiates between two types of grass: kina 'edible grass' and mun 'inedible grass'.","ja":"アイヌ語は2種類の草を厳密に区別しており、kina は「可食の草」、mun は「不可食の草」を指す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kina","mun"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0134-12","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-noun-epuyke-generally-means-flower-but-depending","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--flora"],"statement":{"en":"The noun 'epuyke' generally means 'flower', but depending on context it can also refer to a 'bud' or 'fruit'.","ja":"epuyke は「花」のほか，場合によっては「つぼみ」や「実」のことを指すこともある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["epuyke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0036-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-noun-ipe-usually-refers-to-the-edible","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--flora"],"statement":{"en":"The noun ipe usually refers to the edible fruit or root part of a plant, and its use for animal meat is rare.","ja":"ipe は植物の食用となる実や根の部分を指すのが普通で、動物の肉に対して用いられた例は珍しい。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ipe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0341-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-phrase-ynu-mo-s-r-means-ainu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--geography"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase 'áynu mo-sír means 'Ainu land' and refers to the Ainu ethnic territory.","ja":"’áynu mo-sír という表現は「アイヌの土地」を意味し、アイヌの民族領域を指す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["'áynu mo-sír"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:janhunen2022@handbook-epub/l0010-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-ainu-word-sar-means-field-of-reeds","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--geography"],"statement":{"en":"The Ainu word sar means 'field of reeds'.","ja":"アイヌ語の単語 sar は「ヨシ原」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["sar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:ono2022@handbook-epub/l0080-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--in-modern-ainu-dialects-the-noun-kotan-means","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--geography"],"statement":{"en":"In modern Ainu dialects, the noun kotan means 'village, settlement'.","ja":"現代アイヌ語諸方言において名詞 kotan は「村、集落」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kotan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0039-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-term-ynu-literally-person-man-in-general","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The term 'áynu, literally 'person, man in general, human being', served across all regional Ainu groups as an endonym referring to members of the Ainu ethnic group.","ja":"語 'áynu は文字通りには「人間、一般的な男、人」を意味し、アイヌ民族の成員を指す自称詞としてアイヌの全地域集団に知られていた。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["'áynu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:janhunen2022@handbook-epub/l0010-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--the-phrase-ynu-it-k-refers-to-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase 'áynu 'iták refers to the Ainu language.","ja":"’áynu ’iták という表現はアイヌ語を指す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["'áynu 'iták"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:janhunen2022@handbook-epub/l0010-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--in-the-ainu-language-the-word-aynu-means","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In the Ainu language, the word aynu means 'person'.","ja":"アイヌ語において、aynu という単語は「人」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["aynu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0010-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--in-ainu-uni-denotes-a-house-as-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, uni denotes a house as a place of habitat, whereas cise denotes a house as an actual physical building.","ja":"アイヌ語において uni は居住地としての「家」を表し、cise は実際の物理的建造物としての「家」を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["uni","cise"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:vovin2022@handbook-epub/l0040-08","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--although-speakers-translate-maw-as-wind-in-actual","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topics":["topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis","topic:contact/lexical-semantic-fields-synopsis--weather"],"statement":{"en":"Although speakers translate maw as 'wind', in actual usage it often corresponds to Japanese 'kimochi, kehai, chōkō' (omen, indication, sign, presence).","ja":"maw の意味を話者に尋ねると「風」と答えるが、実際の例では日本語の「気味、気配、兆候」などに当たる場合が多い。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["maw"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0265-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
